<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 22 September, from 904 to 1980.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">904 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhu Wen has Emperor Zhaozong of Tang murdered</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhu-wen">Zhu Wen</a>, who had seized control of the imperial government and moved Emperor Zhaozong to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, had him murdered. Zhaozong was the penultimate Tang emperor; Zhu Wen ended the dynasty in 907, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-liang">Later Liang</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-zhaozong-of-tang">Emperor Zhaozong of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhu-wen">Zhu Wen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1236">1236 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">790 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samogitians and Semigallians defeat the Sword Brethren at Saule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near modern Šiauliai in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, Samogitian and Semigallian forces destroyed an army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> returning from a raid, killing the order's master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volquin">Volkwin</a>. The broken order was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> the next year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saule">Battle of Saule</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitians">Samogitians</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1359">1359 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">667 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aragonese cavalry rout a Castilian force at Araviana</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-two-peters">War of the Two Peters</a>, eight hundred Aragonese horsemen, many of them Castilian exiles under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile">Henry of Trastámara</a>, routed a Castilian frontier force near Ágreda. Its commander, Juan Fernández de Henestrosa, and numerous Castilian nobles and knights were killed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-two-peters">War of the Two Peters</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1499">1499 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">527 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Basel ends the Swabian War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Maximilian I made peace with the Swiss Confederation after its victories in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-war">Swabian War</a>. The Swiss became independent of the Empire in practice; formal recognition came in 1648.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1692">1692 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">334 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The last executions of the Salem witch trials take place</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Martha Corey, Mary Eastey, Alice Parker, Mary Parker, Ann Pudeator, Wilmot Redd, Margaret Scott and Samuel Wardwell were hanged for witchcraft, the last executions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salem-witch-trials">Salem witch trials</a>. Nineteen were hanged in all before Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-phips">William Phips</a> halted the trials.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salem-witch-trials">Salem witch trials</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The British hang Nathan Hale as a spy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Captured behind British lines on Long Island, 21-year-old Captain Nathan Hale was hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>. He is said to have regretted that he had 'but one life to lose for my country'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1862">1862 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln issues the preliminary Emancipation Proclamation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lincoln announced that enslaved people in states still in rebellion on 1 January 1863 would be declared free. The war for the Union became also a war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1980">1980 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">46 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Iraq invades Iran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a>'s forces invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, starting an eight-year war of trenches, missile attacks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poison-gas">poison gas</a>. Hundreds of thousands died before a ceasefire in 1988 left borders unchanged.</p></div></li></ol>
